/**
\defgroup distrib_mvgaussian1 mvgaussian1 (mean, covariance)
\brief Multivariate Gaussian with mean vector \f$\mu\f$ and covariance matrix \f$\Sigma = M(\theta)\f$ given by a matrix structure.

Defined in `<laplace/distrib/mvgaussian1.hpp>` as \ref laplace::distrib::mvgaussian1_distrib "mvgaussian1_distrib\<S\>", in namespace `laplace::distrib`. It follows the interface of \ref distrib_multivariate "Multivariate" (state, derivative blocks, storage orders). Over a positive definite structure `S` it is proper; over a positive semidefinite structure modeling `constant_null_space_psdmat` a partial specialization gives the degenerate class (singular covariance). All evaluation, derivative, information, moment and draw members of the proper class are `LAPLACE_HD`; `start_value()` and the degenerate class run on the host only. Across derivative blocks of orders 0 to 6 over six structures it matches 60-digit mpmath references within 5.6 to 34 ulp1N, and within 118 ulp1N at a near-singular `factor_analytic_pdmat` point.

## Classic form and parametrization

The \f$d\f$-variate normal distribution \f$\mathcal{N}_d(\mu, \Sigma)\f$, with mean \f$\mu \in \mathbb{R}^d\f$, positive definite covariance \f$\Sigma \in \mathbb{R}^{d \times d}\f$ and residual \f$r = y - \mu\f$ for an observation \f$y \in \mathbb{R}^d\f$, has density and log-density
\f[
f_1(y; \mu, \theta) = (2\pi)^{-d/2}\det(\Sigma)^{-1/2}\exp\!\left(-\tfrac{1}{2} r^\top \Sigma^{-1} r\right), \qquad
\ell_1 = -\tfrac{d}{2}\log 2\pi - \tfrac{1}{2}\log\det\Sigma - \tfrac{1}{2} r^\top\Sigma^{-1}r,
\f]
where `mvgaussian1_distrib\<S\>` sets \f$\Sigma = M(\theta)\f$, the matrix of the structure `S` at its parameters \f$\theta\f$.

## State

`theta_state(theta, w)` returns an \ref laplace::distrib::mvgaussian1_state "mvgaussian1_state". It records \f$\log\det\Sigma\f$ from `structure.log_det()`, the matrix of the quadratic form \f$W = \Sigma^{-1}\f$ from `structure.inverse()`, and the lower Cholesky factor \f$L\f$ of \f$\Sigma\f$ (`structure.cholesky()` when `S::closed_factor` is `true`, a Cholesky factorization of `structure.matrix()` otherwise). `state_size()` is \f$2 d(d + 1)/2\f$ doubles and `scratch_size()` is \f$2 d(d + 1)/2\f$ plus `structure.scratch_size()` doubles.

\anchor mvgaussian1_blocks
## Log-density derivative blocks

Let \f$\partial_T\f$ denote the derivative along the sorted index tuple \f$T\f$ of `idx`. The non-trivial blocks of `logpdf_dk<K, A>()` are
\f[
A = 0:\quad -\tfrac{1}{2}\,\partial_T\log\det\Sigma - \tfrac{1}{2} r^\top(\partial_T W)r, \qquad
A = 1:\quad (\partial_T W)r, \qquad
A = 2:\quad -\partial_T W,
\f]
with \f$\partial_T W\f$ from `structure.inverse_dk<K>()` and \f$\partial_T \log\det\Sigma\f$ from `structure.log_det_dk<K>()`. For \f$A \ge 3\f$ every block vanishes and the call returns `false`. `logpdf_dy_dk<J, K>()` returns \f$(-1)^J\f$ times the \f$\mu\f$ block with \f$A = J\f$.

\anchor mvgaussian1_theta_table
## The theta table

When \f$\theta\f$ is shared by the units, the derivatives of \f$W\f$ and \f$\log\det M\f$ can be computed once into a table and attached to the state. Each entry holds `pdmat::packed_size(d) + 2` doubles: a flag (\f$1\f$ when \f$\partial_T W\f$ is not identically zero by structure, \f$0\f$ otherwise), \f$\partial_T \log\det M\f$, and \f$\partial_T W\f$ packed. Entries cover the orders \f$k = 1\f$ to \f$k_{\max}\f$ in turn, and within order \f$k\f$ the \f$\binom{q + k - 1}{k}\f$ sorted \f$k\f$-tuples of \f$\{0, \dots, q - 1\}\f$ (\f$q\f$ = `theta_size()`) in lexicographic order. `theta_table_entries(k_max)` returns the number of entries and `theta_table_size(k_max)` the size of the table in doubles.

`fill_theta_table_entry(st, k_max, entry, table, w)` fills one entry (`0 <= entry < theta_table_entries(k_max)`) with `scratch_size()` doubles in `w`, so a Kokkos kernel can fill all entries in parallel once per \f$\theta\f$. `with_theta_table(st, k_max, table)` returns a copy of `st` with `table` attached and `table_order` set to `k_max`; `table` must remain alive while that state is used.

`logpdf_dk()`, `logpdf_dy_dk()` and the block `(0, 0)` of `expected_info_dk()` read \f$\partial_T \log\det M\f$ and \f$\partial_T W\f$ from the table when \f$1 \le K \le k_{\max}\f$; otherwise, and for the block `(theta_slot, theta_slot)`, they compute from `structure`. The tests in `tests/distrib/test_mvgaussian.cpp` check, over all reference blocks of orders 1 to 3, that the blocks read from a table equal the blocks computed directly to the bit, on gcc/OpenMP and CUDA.

\anchor mvgaussian1_info
## Expected Fisher information

`expected_info_dk<K>(state, slot_a, slot_b, ab, idx, out, w)` writes the order-\f$K\f$ derivative (\f$0 \le K \le 4\f$) of the information block of the slots `slot_a`, `slot_b` (see \ref distrib_multivariate "Multivariate"), with a workspace `w` of at least `info_scratch_size()` doubles. The block `(0, 0)`, \f$(\mu, \mu)\f$, writes the packed matrix \f$\partial_T W\f$ (\f$W\f$ when \f$K = 0\f$). The cross block `(0, theta_slot)`, \f$(\mu, \theta)\f$, vanishes identically by symmetry, and the call returns `false` without touching `out`. The block `(theta_slot, theta_slot)`, \f$(\theta, \theta)\f$, writes the scalar \f$\partial_T I_{ab}\f$ for the parameter pair `ab` = \f$(a, b)\f$, by one of two routes.

Over a structure with `S::closed_factor`, the block `(theta_slot, theta_slot)` evaluates the factor form
\f[
I_{ab} = \tfrac{1}{2}\operatorname{tr}(B_a B_b), \qquad
B_a = G_a + G_a^\top, \qquad
G_a = L^{-1}\partial_a L,
\qquad
\partial_T I_{ab} = \tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{U \subseteq T}\operatorname{tr}\!\big(\partial_U B_a\,\partial_{T \setminus U} B_b\big),
\f]
where \f$U\f$ runs over the subsets of the positions of \f$T\f$. Let \f$L[m]\f$ be the derivative of \f$L\f$ along the indices selected by a mask \f$m\f$ (from `structure.cholesky_dk`), and \f$Y = L^{-1}\f$. For each non-empty mask \f$m\f$ over the positions of \f$(a, b, T)\f$ that does not contain both \f$a\f$ and \f$b\f$, forward substitution solves \f$L\,H[m] = L[m]\f$ for the whitened lower-triangular matrix \f$H[m] = L^{-1} L[m]\f$. For disjoint masks \f$S\f$ and \f$R\f$ over the positions of \f$T\f$, the product \f$X[S, R] = Y[S]\,L[R]\f$, with \f$Y[S]\f$ the \f$S\f$-derivative of \f$Y\f$, follows from
\f[
X[\emptyset, R] = H[R], \qquad
X[S, R] = -\sum_{\emptyset \neq P \subseteq S} H[P]\,X[S \setminus P, R],
\qquad
\partial_S G_a = \sum_{S_1 \subseteq S} X[S_1, \{a\} + (S \setminus S_1)],
\f]
where \f$\{a\} + (S \setminus S_1)\f$ adjoins the position of \f$a\f$ to \f$S \setminus S_1\f$. Every \f$\partial_U G_a\f$ is lower triangular, so each trace is \f$\tfrac{1}{2}\operatorname{tr}(B^{(1)} B^{(2)}) = \sum_i G^{(1)}_{ii} G^{(2)}_{ii} + \sum_{j \le i} G^{(1)}_{ij} G^{(2)}_{ij}\f$. Only products of whitened triangular matrices are formed, so nothing cancels near a singular \f$\Sigma\f$.

\anchor mvgaussian1_trace_route
Over structures without `closed_factor` (such as `factor_analytic_pdmat` and `unstructured_pdmat\<matrix_log_bijector\>`), the block `(theta_slot, theta_slot)` applies Leibniz's rule to the trace form, with \f$V = W^{-1} = \Sigma\f$:
\f[
I_{ab} = \tfrac{1}{2}\,\partial_{ab}\log\det\Sigma + \tfrac{1}{2}\operatorname{tr}\!\big(V\,\partial_{ab}W\big),
\qquad
\partial_T I_{ab} = \tfrac{1}{2}\,\partial_{abT}\log\det\Sigma + \tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{U \subseteq T}\operatorname{tr}\!\big(\partial_U V\;\partial_{ab,\,T\setminus U}W\big).
\f]
No product of the form \f$V(\partial_a W)V(\partial_b W)\f$ is formed. On this route `info_scratch_size()` is \f$2 d(d + 1)/2\f$ plus `structure.scratch_size()` doubles; with the factor form it is the larger of that size and \f$113 d^2 + d(d + 1)/2\f$ plus `structure.scratch_size()` doubles.

\anchor mvgaussian1_draws
## Draws, moments and starting values

`rng(state, mu, seed, unit, y)` writes the draw \f$y = \mu + L z\f$ (\f$\Sigma = L L^\top\f$). Each standard normal coordinate \f$z_k\f$ (\f$k = 0, \dots, d - 1\f$) comes from \ref laplace::distrib::standard_normal_by_inversion "standard_normal_by_inversion()" on the \ref laplace::distrib::counter_uniform_source "counter_uniform_source" `{seed, unit}` (see \ref distrib_generic "Generic routes"), so the draw of a unit depends only on `(seed, unit)`, across threads and backends.

`mean(mu, out)` copies \f$\mu\f$ into `out`, and `covariance(theta, out, w)` writes the packed \f$\Sigma\f$ from `structure.matrix()`, with `structure.scratch_size()` doubles in `w`.

On the host, `start_value(summary, theta)` reads a \ref laplace::distrib::distrib_mv_sample_summary "distrib_mv_sample_summary", floors the eigenvalues of the sample covariance at \f$10^{-6}\f$ times the largest one, and maps the result to \f$\theta\f$ with `structure.params_from_matrix()` (see \ref pdmat "Positive definite structures").

\anchor mvgaussian1_degenerate
## The degenerate class

Over a structure `S` modeling \ref laplace::distrib::constant_null_space_psdmat "constant_null_space_psdmat" (see \ref distrib_multivariate "Multivariate"), the partial specialization of `mvgaussian1_distrib\<S\>` sets `normalization` to `distrib_normalization::degenerate` and runs on the host only. With \f$\Sigma = M(\theta)\f$ of rank \f$\rho\f$ (returned by `rank()`), \f$\lvert\cdot\rvert_+\f$ the pseudo-determinant (the product of the \f$\rho\f$ nonzero eigenvalues) and \f$\Sigma^+\f$ the Moore-Penrose pseudo-inverse, it is a proper law on \f$\mu + \operatorname{col}\Sigma\f$ with log-density
\f[
\ell_1 = -\tfrac{\rho}{2}\log 2\pi - \tfrac{1}{2}\log\lvert\Sigma\rvert_+ - \tfrac{1}{2} r^\top \Sigma^+ r
\f]
on the support and \f$-\infty\f$ off it. Let \f$U_0\f$ be the \f$d \times (d - \rho)\f$ orthonormal basis of the null space; \f$y\f$ is off the support when \f$\lVert U_0^\top r\rVert > 64\,d\,\varepsilon\,\lVert r\rVert\f$, with \f$\varepsilon = 2^{-52}\f$. Only the value (`logpdf()` and the block \f$A = K = 0\f$) applies this test; the derivative blocks are those of the density on the range.

\anchor mvgaussian1_pseudo_inverse
### Pseudo-inverse and its derivatives

Let \f$P = U_0 U_0^\top\f$ be the orthogonal projector onto the null space. For any fixed \f$c > 0\f$,
\f[
\Sigma^+ = (\Sigma + cP)^{-1} - \frac{P}{c}.
\f]
The state takes \f$c = \operatorname{tr}\Sigma / \rho\f$ at its \f$\theta\f$ (\f$1\f$ when \f$\rho = 0\f$ or \f$\operatorname{tr}\Sigma \le 0\f$) and keeps it fixed while differentiating, so \f$\partial_T \Sigma^+ = \partial_T(\Sigma + cP)^{-1}\f$ for every non-empty tuple \f$T\f$. With \f$A = (\Sigma + cP)^{-1}\f$, \f$A_Q\f$ its derivative along a subset \f$Q\f$ of the positions, and \f$M_T\f$ the derivative of the structure along \f$T\f$, the implementation evaluates recursively
\f[
A_Q = -A \sum_{\emptyset \ne T \subseteq Q} M_T\,A_{Q \setminus T}.
\f]

\anchor mvgaussian1_rank_deficient_state
### State, blocks and information

`theta_state(theta, w)` returns an \ref laplace::distrib::mvgaussian_rank_deficient_state "mvgaussian_rank_deficient_state", the state of both singular classes (this one and the improper class of \ref distrib_mvgaussian2 "mvgaussian2"). It records \f$\log\lvert M\rvert_+\f$ from `structure.log_pdet_state()`, keeping the structure's evaluated state in `w` so that every derivative of \f$\log\lvert M\rvert_+\f$ is read with `log_pdet_dk_at()`; the matrix of the quadratic form; and, for this class, the Cholesky factor of \f$\Sigma + cP\f$ and \f$(\Sigma + cP)^{-1}\f$. `state_size()` is \f$3\,d(d + 1)/2\f$ plus `structure.scratch_size()` doubles. The \f$\theta\f$ table works as in the proper class, except that entries are filled one at a time, because they share the structure's evaluated state.

`logpdf_dk<K, A>()` and `logpdf_dy_dk<J, K>()` are the blocks of the proper class with \f$\Sigma^+\f$ in place of \f$W\f$ and \f$\log\lvert\Sigma\rvert_+\f$ in place of \f$\log\det\Sigma\f$.

`expected_info_dk<K>()` (\f$K \le 4\f$) exists only for structures with \f$\partial_{ab} M = \delta_{ab}\,\partial_a M\f$, in which each term is linear in its own \f$e^{\theta_j}\f$ (today `weighted_sum_psdmat`). The block `(0, 0)` writes \f$\Sigma^+\f$ and its \f$\theta\f$-derivatives, and the block `(0, theta_slot)` returns `false`. The block `(theta_slot, theta_slot)` evaluates
\f[
I_{ab} = -\tfrac{1}{2}\,\partial_{ab}\log\lvert M\rvert_+ + \tfrac{1}{2}\,\delta_{ab}\,\partial_a\log\lvert M\rvert_+,
\f]
which equals \f$\tfrac{1}{2}\operatorname{tr}(B_a B_b)\f$ with \f$B_a\f$ similar to \f$e^{\theta_a} M^+ S_a\f$, \f$S_a\f$ the \f$a\f$-th component matrix of the structure, and differentiates the right-hand side for the \f$\theta\f$-derivatives. The trace form of the proper class is not offered: evaluated through \f$M^+\f$ it cancels catastrophically, up to \f$1.8 \times 10^{17}\f$ ulp1N when the components of \f$\theta\f$ are 9 apart.

### Draws, moments and starting values

`rng(state, mu, seed, unit, y, tmp)` takes `tmp` of `dim()` doubles and writes \f$y = \mu + (I - P) L z\f$, with \f$\Sigma + cP = L L^\top\f$ and \f$z\f$ as in the proper class; its covariance is \f$(I - P)(\Sigma + cP)(I - P) = \Sigma\f$. The class also provides `mean()` and `covariance()`. On the host, `start_value(summary, theta)` projects the sample covariance \f$C\f$ onto the range, \f$C_p = (I - P) C (I - P)\f$, without the eigenvalue floor of the proper class (which would put mass on the null space), and passes \f$C_p\f$ to `structure.params_from_matrix()`.

\anchor mvgaussian1_accuracy
## Accuracy

The method is on \ref accuracy "How accuracy is measured". Reference values (`tools/reference/distrib_mvgaussian.py`, `tests/data/reference/mvgaussian.csv`) were computed with mpmath (The mpmath development team, 2023) at 60 digits from the definitions (checked against 75 digits to \f$10^{-40}(1 + |v|)\f$): 5693 values for both parametrizations, over six structures (`diagonal_pdmat`, `ar1_pdmat`, `compound_symmetry_pdmat`, `unstructured_pdmat\<log_cholesky_bijector\>`, `unit_diagonal_scaled_pdmat\<ar1_pdmat\>`, and `factor_analytic_pdmat` with one factor) at \f$d \in \{2, 3, 4, 5\}\f$, one random point and one hard point per structure. Errors are in `ulp1N`, the largest entry error over a block in units of \f$\mathrm{ulp}(\max(S_{\mathrm{block}}, 1))\f$, where \f$S_{\mathrm{block}}\f$ is the largest reference magnitude over every tuple and entry of that point, \f$A\f$ and \f$K\f$ (and at least the largest \f$|I_{ab}|\f$ at that point for the information). Blocks cover \f$A \in \{0, 1, 2\}\f$ up to total order 6, the information orders 0 to 4; bounds are those of `tests/distrib/test_mvgaussian.cpp` on gcc/OpenMP and CUDA (RTX 4070 SUPER).

| Structures | Blocks gcc (CUDA), bound | Information gcc (CUDA), bound |
|---|---|---|
| diagonal, CS, log-Cholesky, scaled AR(1) | 5.6 (5.6), 1–9 | 0 (0) diag. / 1.25 (1.25) log-Chol. / 1.35 (1.35) CS / 11.6 (11.6) scaled AR(1), bounds 1 / 2 / 1–3 / 3–18 |
| `ar1_pdmat` | 34 (22), 52 | 16.4 (16.3), 2–25 |
| `factor_analytic_pdmat` | 118 (78.9), 1–180 | 33.1 (12.1), 3–50 |

The largest error is at the `factor_analytic_pdmat` hard point (\f$\psi = e^{-6}\f$): the \f$A = 0\f$, order-5 block, which goes through `factor_analytic_pdmat::inverse_dk`, reaches 118 ulp1N, where \ref distrib_mvgaussian2 "mvgaussian2", which uses `matrix_dk`, stays within 1.3 ulp1N.

For `diagonal_pdmat` and `unstructured_pdmat\<matrix_log_bijector\>`, where \f$M(-\theta) = M(\theta)^{-1}\f$, the tests compare `mvgaussian1_distrib\<S\>` at \f$\theta\f$ with `mvgaussian2_distrib\<S\>` at \f$-\theta\f$: every block and the information agree up to the sign \f$(-1)^K\f$ (0 ulp1N on gcc, 0.7 on CUDA, bound 1). The tests also check central differences at orders 5–6 and information orders 1–4 (within \f$10^{-6}\f$ of the scales of orders \f$K\f$ and \f$K - 1\f$, \f$10^{-5}\f$ for `factor_analytic_pdmat`), \f$2 \times 10^5\f$ device draws (mean, covariance and score-Hessian checks within 1.2 standard errors, bound 5), and the covariance recovered by `start_value()` (within \f$10^{-12}\f$ relative for `log_cholesky_bijector`).

For the singular classes over `weighted_sum_psdmat`, 5215 reference values (`tools/reference/distrib_mvgaussian_rank_deficient.py`, `tests/data/reference/mvgaussian_rank_deficient.csv`) were computed with mpmath at 60 digits from the eigendecomposition, over four difference-penalty structures (\f$d \in \{4, 5, 6\}\f$, one random point and one spread point with \f$\theta\f$ components 9 apart per structure), and checked in `tests/distrib/test_mvgaussian_rank_deficient.cpp`, with the same results on gcc 14.2 and the host code of the CUDA (MSVC) build. For the degenerate class:

| Points | Blocks (\f$A = 0, 1, 2\f$), bound | Information, bound |
|---|---|---|
| random | 117, bound 176 | 1.12, bound 4 |
| spread (\f$d = 5\f$, two penalties) | \f$4.86 \times 10^6\f$, bound \f$7.3 \times 10^6\f$ | \f$2.4 \times 10^{-4}\f$, bound 4 |
| spread (\f$d = 6\f$, three penalties) | \f$3.28 \times 10^{12}\f$ (\f$A = 0\f$: \f$1.15 \times 10^{11}\f$, \f$A = 1\f$: \f$7.15 \times 10^{11}\f$), bound \f$4.9 \times 10^{12}\f$ | 0.25, bound 4 |

The dense \f$(\Sigma + cP)^{-1}\f$ loses accuracy in proportion to the condition number of \f$\Sigma\f$ on its range, which grows when the weights \f$\lambda_j = e^{\theta_j}\f$ are spread: \f$2.07 \times 10^5\f$ at the \f$d = 5\f$ spread point and \f$6.53 \times 10^9\f$ at the \f$d = 6\f$ one. The errors are 24 and 500 times that number times \f$\varepsilon\f$, about \f$7 \times 10^{-4}\f$ relative at the worst point. The tests also check \f$-\infty\f$ off the support, 40,000 draws (null-space component below \f$10^{-12}\f$, covariance within 6 standard errors) and the parameters recovered by `start_value()` (within \f$10^{-10}\f$). The full breakdown is in `docs/numerics.md`.

\anchor mvgaussian1_speed
## Speed

Times from `benchmarks/distrib_mvgaussian.cpp`, over \f$n = 10^5\f$ units with `unstructured_pdmat\<log_cholesky_bijector\>`, in nanoseconds per unit: order 0 (`logpdf()`), order 1 (the gradient in \f$\mu\f$ and all \f$\theta_j\f$) and order 2 (all order-2 blocks), on OpenMP (16 threads) and CUDA (RTX 4070 SUPER), without a \f$\theta\f$ table.

| \f$d\f$ | Mode | Order 0 OpenMP / CUDA (ns) | Order 1 OpenMP / CUDA (ns) | Order 2 OpenMP / CUDA (ns) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2 | Shared \f$\theta\f$ | 1.5 / 0.3 | 32 / 6.8 | 128 / 31 |
| 2 | Per-unit \f$\theta\f$ | 9.6 / 1.2 | 39 / 7.6 | 135 / 32 |
| 3 | Shared \f$\theta\f$ | 1.6 / 0.3 | 77 / 25 | 570 / 210 |
| 3 | Per-unit \f$\theta\f$ | 17 / 2.1 | 89 / 27 | 592 / 212 |
| 5 | Shared \f$\theta\f$ | 3.2 / 0.6 | 342 / 209 | 6217 / 4050 |
| 5 | Per-unit \f$\theta\f$ | 34 / 7.1 | 367 / 236 | 6316 / 4434 |
| 10 | Shared \f$\theta\f$ | 8.8 / 2.0 | 4526 / 3412 | \f$2.50 \times 10^5\f$ / \f$2.40 \times 10^5\f$ |
| 10 | Per-unit \f$\theta\f$ | 84 / 28 | 4161 / 3489 | \f$2.46 \times 10^5\f$ / \f$2.42 \times 10^5\f$ |

With an order-2 \f$\theta\f$ table attached (shared \f$\theta\f$), together with the time to fill the table, paid once per \f$\theta\f$:

| \f$d\f$ | Order 1 OpenMP / CUDA (ns) | Order 2 OpenMP / CUDA (ns) | Order-2 fill OpenMP / CUDA (\f$\mu\f$s) |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2 | 3.7 / 0.5 | 8.3 / 0.9 | 81 / 35 |
| 3 | 7.2 / 0.9 | 27 / 3.0 | 71 / 45 |
| 5 | 27 / 3.7 | 188 / 29 | 96 / 119 |
| 10 | 158 / 36 | 4775 / 1002 | 414 / 497 |

For `logpdf()`, sharing \f$\theta\f$ costs \f$O(d^2)\f$ per unit, whereas a state per unit costs \f$O(d^3)\f$ (6 to 14 times slower at \f$d = 10\f$). Without a table, each block with \f$K \ge 1\f$ recomputes \f$\partial_T W = \partial_T \Sigma^{-1}\f$, so at \f$d = 10\f$, order 2, this parametrization takes 120 times longer on OpenMP and 265 times longer on CUDA than \ref distrib_mvgaussian2 "mvgaussian2". With the table each unit pays \f$O(d^2)\f$ per tuple, and the gap falls to a factor of 2.4 on OpenMP and 4.1 on CUDA.

For the degenerate class over `weighted_sum_psdmat` with the difference-penalty sum \f$(D_1^\top D_1, D_2^\top D_2, D_3^\top D_3)\f$ of rank \f$d - 1\f$, host times in seconds (one thread, gcc 14.2, median of 5 calls at \f$d = 500\f$, one call at \f$d = 2000\f$) from `benchmarks/distrib_mvgaussian_rank_deficient.cpp`:

| Operation | \f$d = 500\f$ (s) | \f$d = 2000\f$ (s) |
|---|---|---|
| `theta_state()` | 0.41 | 35.4 |
| `logpdf()` | \f$6.4 \times 10^{-5}\f$ | \f$1.3 \times 10^{-3}\f$ |
| \f$A = 1, K = 0\f$ | \f$1.3 \times 10^{-4}\f$ | \f$3.3 \times 10^{-3}\f$ |
| \f$A = 0, K = 1\f$ | 0.040 | 4.1 |
| \f$A = 0, K = 2\f$ | 0.12 | 13.3 |
| \f$\theta\f$ table, orders 1–2 (9 entries) | 0.86 | 78.6 |

`theta_state()` costs about the structure's `log_pdet()` alone (0.37 s at \f$d = 500\f$, 28.3 s at \f$d = 2000\f$).

## Example

The example on \ref distrib_mvgaussian2 "mvgaussian2" applies unchanged with `mvgaussian1_distrib` and `mvgaussian1_state` in place of `mvgaussian2_distrib` and `mvgaussian2_state`.

## Module types

- \ref laplace::distrib::mvgaussian1_distrib "mvgaussian1_distrib\<S\>" — multivariate Gaussian with covariance \f$\Sigma = M(\theta)\f$, and its degenerate specialization
- \ref laplace::distrib::mvgaussian1_state "mvgaussian1_state" — state of the proper class at fixed \f$\theta\f$
- \ref laplace::distrib::mvgaussian_rank_deficient_state "mvgaussian_rank_deficient_state" — state of the degenerate class (and of the improper class of mvgaussian2) at fixed \f$\theta\f$

## References

- The mpmath development team (2023), mpmath: a Python library for arbitrary-precision floating-point arithmetic, version 1.3.0, https://mpmath.org
*/

/**
\defgroup distrib_mvgaussian2 mvgaussian2 (mean, precision)
\brief Multivariate Gaussian with mean vector \f$\mu\f$ and precision matrix \f$Q = M(\theta)\f$ given by a matrix structure.

Defined in `<laplace/distrib/mvgaussian2.hpp>` as \ref laplace::distrib::mvgaussian2_distrib "mvgaussian2_distrib\<S\>", in namespace `laplace::distrib`. It follows the interface of \ref distrib_multivariate "Multivariate". Over a positive definite structure `S` it is proper; over a positive semidefinite structure modeling `constant_null_space_psdmat` a partial specialization gives the improper class (singular precision). All evaluation, derivative, information, moment and draw members of the proper class are `LAPLACE_HD`; `start_value()` and the improper class run on the host only. Across derivative blocks of orders 0 to 6 over six structures it matches 60-digit mpmath references within 9.0 ulp1N.

## Classic form and parametrization

With the precision \f$Q = \Sigma^{-1} = M(\theta)\f$ in place of the covariance of \ref distrib_mvgaussian1 "mvgaussian1", the density and log-density of \f$\mathcal{N}_d(\mu, Q^{-1})\f$ are
\f[
f_2(y; \mu, \theta) = (2\pi)^{-d/2}\det(Q)^{1/2}\exp\!\left(-\tfrac{1}{2} r^\top Q r\right), \qquad
\ell_2 = -\tfrac{d}{2}\log 2\pi + \tfrac{1}{2}\log\det Q - \tfrac{1}{2} r^\top Q r,
\f]
with \f$r = y - \mu\f$. The quadratic form uses \f$M(\theta)\f$ directly, so no inverse is formed to evaluate the density or its derivatives.

## State

`theta_state(theta, w)` returns an \ref laplace::distrib::mvgaussian2_state "mvgaussian2_state". It records \f$\log\det Q\f$ from `structure.log_det()`, the matrix of the quadratic form \f$W = Q\f$ from `structure.matrix()`, and the lower Cholesky factor \f$L\f$ of \f$Q\f$ (`structure.cholesky()` when `S::closed_factor` is `true`, a Cholesky factorization of `structure.matrix()` otherwise). `state_size()` is \f$2 d(d + 1)/2\f$ doubles and `scratch_size()` is \f$2 d(d + 1)/2\f$ plus `structure.scratch_size()` doubles.

## Log-density derivative blocks

The non-trivial blocks of `logpdf_dk<K, A>()` are
\f[
A = 0:\quad \tfrac{1}{2}\,\partial_T\log\det Q - \tfrac{1}{2} r^\top(\partial_T Q)r, \qquad
A = 1:\quad (\partial_T Q)r, \qquad
A = 2:\quad -\partial_T Q,
\f]
with \f$\partial_T Q\f$ from `structure.matrix_dk<K>()` and \f$\partial_T \log\det Q\f$ from `structure.log_det_dk<K>()`. For \f$A \ge 3\f$ every block vanishes and the call returns `false`; `logpdf_dy_dk<J, K>()` returns \f$(-1)^J\f$ times the \f$\mu\f$ block with \f$A = J\f$. The \f$\theta\f$ table is the one described on \ref mvgaussian1_theta_table "mvgaussian1", with \f$W = Q\f$.

## Expected Fisher information

`expected_info_dk<K>()` (\f$K \le 4\f$) has the blocks described on \ref mvgaussian1_info "mvgaussian1": the block `(0, 0)` writes \f$\partial_T Q\f$ (\f$Q\f$ when \f$K = 0\f$) and the block `(0, theta_slot)` returns `false`. The block `(theta_slot, theta_slot)` always takes the trace route (\ref mvgaussian1_trace_route "Leibniz's rule on the trace"), with \f$V = Q^{-1}\f$:
\f[
I_{ab} = -\tfrac{1}{2}\,\partial_{ab}\log\det Q + \tfrac{1}{2}\operatorname{tr}\!\big(V\,\partial_{ab}Q\big),
\qquad
\partial_T I_{ab} = -\tfrac{1}{2}\,\partial_{abT}\log\det Q + \tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{U \subseteq T}\operatorname{tr}\!\big(\partial_U V\;\partial_{ab,\,T\setminus U}Q\big).
\f]
`info_scratch_size()` is \f$2 d(d + 1)/2\f$ plus `structure.scratch_size()` doubles.

## Draws, moments and starting values

`rng(state, mu, seed, unit, y)` writes \f$y = \mu + L^{-\top} z\f$ (\f$Q = L L^\top\f$), with the standard normal \f$z\f$ generated as on \ref mvgaussian1_draws "mvgaussian1". `mean(mu, out)` copies \f$\mu\f$, and `covariance(theta, out, w)` writes the packed \f$Q^{-1}\f$ from `structure.inverse()`, with `structure.scratch_size()` doubles in `w`. On the host, `start_value(summary, theta)` floors the eigenvalues of the sample covariance at \f$10^{-6}\f$ times the largest one, inverts the result, and maps it to \f$\theta\f$ with `structure.params_from_matrix()`.

## The improper class

Over a structure `S` modeling \ref laplace::distrib::constant_null_space_psdmat "constant_null_space_psdmat" (see \ref distrib_multivariate "Multivariate"), the partial specialization of `mvgaussian2_distrib\<S\>` sets `normalization` to `distrib_normalization::improper` and runs on the host only. With a singular precision \f$Q = M(\theta)\f$ of rank \f$\rho\f$ and \f$\lvert\cdot\rvert_+\f$ the pseudo-determinant, the density is flat along the null space of \f$Q\f$, with log-density
\f[
\ell_2 = -\tfrac{\rho}{2}\log 2\pi + \tfrac{1}{2}\log\lvert Q\rvert_+ - \tfrac{1}{2} r^\top Q r.
\f]
The normalizing constant counts only the \f$\rho\f$ dimensions of the range. The quadratic form uses \f$Q\f$ directly, so the density needs no pseudo-inverse.

`theta_state(theta, w)` returns the \ref mvgaussian1_rank_deficient_state "mvgaussian_rank_deficient_state" of the singular classes, without a factor. `constrained_state(theta, w)` returns the same state with the Cholesky factor of \f$Q + cP\f$ and \f$(Q + cP)^{-1}\f$ added, where \f$P\f$ is the projector onto the null space and \f$c = \operatorname{tr} Q / \rho\f$ (see \ref mvgaussian1_pseudo_inverse "the pseudo-inverse on mvgaussian1"). The derivative blocks are those of the proper class with \f$\log\lvert Q\rvert_+\f$ in place of \f$\log\det Q\f$, and the \f$\theta\f$ table is filled one entry at a time.

`expected_info_dk<K>()` exists for the same structures and with the same `(theta_slot, theta_slot)` formula as the \ref mvgaussian1_rank_deficient_state "degenerate class" (the block `(0, 0)` writes \f$Q\f$ and its derivatives). For this class it is the information of the constrained law \f$U_0^\top(y - \mu) = 0\f$, with \f$U_0\f$ an orthonormal basis of the null space. The trace form of the proper class, evaluated through \f$M^+\f$, would reach \f$9.5 \times 10^{11}\f$ ulp1N when the components of \f$\theta\f$ are 9 apart, and is not offered.

The class has no `rng()`, `mean()` or `covariance()`. For the constrained proper law \f$U_0^\top(y - \mu) = 0\f$, whose covariance is \f$Q^+\f$, it provides `constrained_rng(cstate, mu, seed, unit, y, tmp)`, which writes \f$y = \mu + (I - P) L^{-\top} z\f$ with \f$Q + cP = L L^\top\f$, and `constrained_covariance(cstate, out)`, which writes \f$Q^+ = (Q + cP)^{-1} - P/c\f$; both take a state from `constrained_state()`. It also provides `constrained_mean(mu, out)`, which copies \f$\mu\f$ into `out`. On the host, `start_value(summary, theta)` projects the sample covariance \f$C\f$ onto the range, \f$C_p = (I - P) C (I - P)\f$, and passes its pseudo-inverse \f$C_p^+\f$ to `structure.params_from_matrix()`.

## Accuracy

References, structures and the error measure are those of \ref mvgaussian1_accuracy "mvgaussian1"; bounds are those of `tests/distrib/test_mvgaussian.cpp` on gcc/OpenMP and CUDA (RTX 4070 SUPER).

| Structures | Blocks gcc (CUDA), bound | Information gcc (CUDA), bound |
|---|---|---|
| all six | 9.0 (4.0), 1–14 | 129 (33.2) AR(1) / 3.98 rest, 1–200 AR(1) / 1–6 rest |

At the `factor_analytic_pdmat` hard point, where \ref distrib_mvgaussian1 "mvgaussian1" reaches 118 ulp1N through `inverse_dk`, this parametrization stays within 1.3 ulp1N. The comparison with mvgaussian1 at \f$-\theta\f$ and the other checks are described on \ref mvgaussian1_accuracy "mvgaussian1".

For the improper class, over the references of the singular classes described there: blocks within 4 ulp1N for \f$A = 0\f$ and 1 ulp1N for \f$A = 1, 2\f$ (bounds 6 and 4) and information within 1.12 ulp1N (bound 4), at every point, the spread points included, because the blocks never form an inverse. The tests also check \f$Q Q^+ Q = Q\f$ within \f$10^{-12} \max\lvert Q\rvert\f$.

## Speed

Measured as on \ref mvgaussian1_speed "mvgaussian1", without a \f$\theta\f$ table:

| \f$d\f$ | Mode | Order 0 OpenMP / CUDA (ns) | Order 1 OpenMP / CUDA (ns) | Order 2 OpenMP / CUDA (ns) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2 | Shared \f$\theta\f$ | 1.7 / 0.3 | 9.5 / 1.2 | 15 / 2.1 |
| 2 | Per-unit \f$\theta\f$ | 7.6 / 0.8 | 12 / 1.5 | 18 / 2.5 |
| 3 | Shared \f$\theta\f$ | 2.2 / 0.3 | 18 / 3.0 | 41 / 7.2 |
| 3 | Per-unit \f$\theta\f$ | 12 / 1.3 | 24 / 4.2 | 47 / 8.0 |
| 5 | Shared \f$\theta\f$ | 3.8 / 0.5 | 48 / 17 | 163 / 52 |
| 5 | Per-unit \f$\theta\f$ | 21 / 3.5 | 59 / 20 | 180 / 57 |
| 10 | Shared \f$\theta\f$ | 7.6 / 1.9 | 267 / 185 | 2070 / 908 |
| 10 | Per-unit \f$\theta\f$ | 51 / 12 | 301 / 197 | 2284 / 915 |

With an order-2 \f$\theta\f$ table attached (shared \f$\theta\f$):

| \f$d\f$ | Order 1 OpenMP / CUDA (ns) | Order 2 OpenMP / CUDA (ns) | Order-2 fill OpenMP / CUDA (\f$\mu\f$s) |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2 | 3.4 / 0.5 | 7.0 / 0.7 | 90 / 13 |
| 3 | 7.9 / 1.0 | 21 / 2.0 | 95 / 14 |
| 5 | 22 / 3.7 | 119 / 12 | 102 / 15 |
| 10 | 157 / 35 | 1953 / 245 | 70 / 17 |

For the improper class, on the structure and with the timing of the \ref mvgaussian1_speed "degenerate class":

| Operation | \f$d = 500\f$ (s) | \f$d = 2000\f$ (s) |
|---|---|---|
| `theta_state()` | 0.39 | 31.7 |
| `constrained_state()` | 0.42 | 36.8 |
| `logpdf()` | \f$6.7 \times 10^{-5}\f$ | \f$1.4 \times 10^{-3}\f$ |
| \f$A = 1, K = 0\f$ | \f$1.4 \times 10^{-4}\f$ | \f$5.9 \times 10^{-3}\f$ |
| \f$A = 0, K = 1\f$ | \f$1.2 \times 10^{-4}\f$ | \f$4.0 \times 10^{-3}\f$ |
| \f$A = 0, K = 2\f$ | \f$1.7 \times 10^{-3}\f$ | 0.036 |
| \f$\theta\f$ table, orders 1–2 (9 entries) | 0.010 | 0.20 |

`theta_state()` costs about the structure's `log_pdet()` alone (0.38 s at \f$d = 500\f$, 32.2 s at \f$d = 2000\f$).

## Example

The following example computes a shared precision state once on the device, fills a \f$\theta\f$ table of order 1 in parallel across its entries, attaches the table to the state, and evaluates `logpdf()` and the first-order derivative blocks over the units:

\code{.cpp}
#include <Kokkos_Core.hpp>
#include <laplace/distrib/mvgaussian2.hpp>
#include <laplace/pdmat/ar1.hpp>

void eval_mvgaussian(const Kokkos::View<const double**>& y,
                     const Kokkos::View<const double**>& mu,
                     const Kokkos::View<const double*>& theta,
                     Kokkos::View<double*>& log_lik,
                     Kokkos::View<double**>& grad_mu,
                     Kokkos::View<double**>& grad_theta) {
  constexpr int d = 3;
  const int n = static_cast<int>(y.extent(0));
  const laplace::distrib::mvgaussian2_distrib<laplace::pdmat::ar1_pdmat> dist(laplace::pdmat::ar1_pdmat(d));
  Kokkos::View<double*> state_buf("state_buf", dist.state_size() + dist.scratch_size());
  Kokkos::View<laplace::distrib::mvgaussian2_state> state_view("state");

  Kokkos::parallel_for(
      "mv_state", 1, KOKKOS_LAMBDA(int) { state_view() = dist.theta_state(theta.data(), state_buf.data()); });

  const int n_entries = dist.theta_table_entries(1);
  Kokkos::View<double*> table_buf("table_buf", dist.theta_table_size(1));
  Kokkos::View<double**, Kokkos::LayoutRight> fill_work("fill_work", n_entries, dist.scratch_size());

  Kokkos::parallel_for(
      "mv_table", n_entries, KOKKOS_LAMBDA(int e) {
        dist.fill_theta_table_entry(state_view(), 1, e, table_buf.data(), &fill_work(e, 0));
      });

  Kokkos::parallel_for(
      "mv_attach", 1, KOKKOS_LAMBDA(int) {
        state_view() = dist.with_theta_table(state_view(), 1, table_buf.data());
      });

  Kokkos::parallel_for(
      "mv_eval", n, KOKKOS_LAMBDA(int i) {
        constexpr int scratch_cap = 2 * laplace::pdmat::packed_size(d);
        double w[scratch_cap];
        double g[d];
        const auto st = state_view();
        log_lik(i) = dist.logpdf(st, &y(i, 0), &mu(i, 0));
        if (dist.template logpdf_dk<0, 1>(st, &y(i, 0), &mu(i, 0), nullptr, g, w)) {
          for (int k = 0; k < d; ++k) grad_mu(i, k) = g[k];
        }
        const int idx[1] = {0};
        double dth = 0.0;
        if (dist.template logpdf_dk<1, 0>(st, &y(i, 0), &mu(i, 0), idx, &dth, w)) {
          grad_theta(i, 0) = dth;
        }
      });
}
\endcode

## Module types

- \ref laplace::distrib::mvgaussian2_distrib "mvgaussian2_distrib\<S\>" — multivariate Gaussian with precision \f$Q = M(\theta)\f$, and its improper specialization
- \ref laplace::distrib::mvgaussian2_state "mvgaussian2_state" — state of the proper class at fixed \f$\theta\f$
*/
